        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Julia Agrippina, most commonly referred to as Agrippina Minor or Agrippina the Younger, and after 50 known as Julia Augusta Agrippina (7 November 15 or 6 November 16 – 19/23 March 59) was a Roman Empress. She was a great-granddaughter of Augustus, great-niece and adoptive granddaughter of Tiberius, sister of Caligula, niece and fourth wife of Claudius, and mother of Nero.</skos:definition>
