        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Annia Faustina</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Annia Aurelia Faustina (c. AD 201 – c. AD 222) was an Anatolian Roman noblewoman. She was briefly married to the Roman emperor Elagabalus in 221 and thus a Roman empress. She was Elagabalus' third wife.</skos:definition>
