        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Diadumenianus</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Diadumenian (Marcus Opellius Antoninus Diadumenianus; 14/19 September 208 – 218), was briefly Roman Emperor from May to June 218. He was born to Macrinus, his father, of which he was co-emperor, and Nonia Celsa, whose name may be fictitious, on 14 September 208.</skos:definition>
