        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Domitia Longina</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="es">Domicia Longina</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Domitia Longina (c. AD 53-55–c. AD 126-130) was an Empress of Rome and wife to the Roman Emperor Domitian. She was the youngest daughter of the general and consul Gnaeus Domitius Corbulo. She became Empress of Rome upon Domitian's accession in 81, and remained so until his assassination in 96.</skos:definition>
