        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Domitius Alexander</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Lucius Domitius Alexander (died c. 311), probably born in Phrygia, was vicarius of Africa when Emperor Maxentius ordered him to send his son as hostage to Rome. Alexander refused and proclaimed himself emperor in 308.</skos:definition>
