        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="pl">Germanik</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Germanicus Julius Caesar (24 May 15 BC – 10 October AD 19), commonly known as Germanicus, was a member of the Julio-Claudian dynasty and a prominent general of the early Roman Empire. He was the great-nephew of the Augustus, nephew and adoptive son of Tiberius, father of Caligula, brother of Claudius, and grandfather of Nero.</skos:definition>
