        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="it">Giusta Grata Onoria</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Justa Grata Honoria, commonly referred to during her lifetime as Honoria, was the daughter of the Roman emperor Constantius III and older sister of Valentinian III. She is famous for her plea of love and help to Attila the Hun, which led to his proclamation of his claim to rule the Western Roman Empire.</skos:definition>
