      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Janus</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">In ancient Roman religion and myth, Janus is the god of beginnings, gates, transitions, time, duality, doorways, passages, frames, and endings. He is usually depicted as having two faces.</skos:definition>
