        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Julia Mamaea</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Julia Avita Mamaea (14 or 29 August after 180–235) was the second daughter of Julia Maesa, a powerful Roman woman of Syrian origin, and Syrian noble Gaius Julius Avitus Alexianus. She was a niece of empress Julia Domna; emperor Lucius Septimius Severus and sister of Julia Soaemias Bassiana. She was born and raised in Emesa (modern Homs, Syria).</skos:definition>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Julia_Avita_Mamaea"/>
