        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="pl">Leon II (cesarz bizantyński)</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Flavius Leo II was briefly the Byzantine (East Roman) emperor in 474 AD when he was a child aged 7. He was the son of Zeno, the Isaurian general and future emperor, and Ariadne, the daughter of Emperor Leo I. Leo II was made co-emperor with his grandfather Leo I on 18 November 473, and became sole emperor on 18 January 474 after Leo I died of dysentery.</skos:definition>
