        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Leontius</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Leontius was a general of the Eastern Roman Empire and claimant to the throne who led a rebellion against emperor Zeno in 484–488.</skos:definition>
