      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Annia Aurelia Galeria Lucilla or Lucilla (March 7, 148 or 150–182) was a daughter of Marcus Aurelius and Faustina the Younger and sister to Commodus. Commodus ordered Lucilla's execution after a failed assassination attempt.</skos:definition>
