        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Mars</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">In ancient Roman religion and myth, Mars was the god of war and also an agricultural guardian, a combination characteristic of early Rome. He was the son of Jupiter and Juno, and he was the most prominent of the military gods in the religion of the Roman army.</skos:definition>
