        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Flavius Odoacer (or Odovacer) was a Germanic soldier, who became the first King of Italy (476-493). He deposed Romulus Augustulus and established a client state to the Zeno of the Eastern Roman Empire.</skos:definition>
