        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Anicius Petronius Maximus (c. 397 – 31 May 455) was Roman emperor of the West for two and a half months in 455. His wife was Licinia Eudoxia, the daughter of Theodosius II, making him a Theodosian dynast by marriage.</skos:definition>
