        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Providentia</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">In ancient Roman religion, Providentia is a divine personification of the ability to foresee and make provision. She was among the embodiments of virtues that were part of the Imperial cult of ancient Rome.</skos:definition>
