        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Lucius Cornelius Sulla Felix (c. 138 BC – 78 BC), known commonly as Sulla, was a Roman general and statesman. He was consul in 88 BC and 80 BC reviving the dictatorship and appointed in 82/1 Bc as dictator legibus faciendis et reipublicae constituendae causa.</skos:definition>
