        <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Theodosius II</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Flavius Theodosius II commonly called Theodosius the Younger, or the Calligrapher, was the Eastern Roman Emperor for most of his life, proclaimed augustus as an infant in 402 and ruling as the Eastern Empire's sole emperor after the death of his father Arcadius in 408.</skos:definition>
