        <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Venus</skos:prefLabel>
        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Venus is a Roman goddess, whose functions encompassed love, beauty, desire, sex, fertility, prosperity, and victory. In Roman mythology, she was the ancestor of the Roman people through her son, Aeneas, who survived the fall of Troy and fled to Italy.</skos:definition>
