        <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Vetranio (died c. 356) was a Roman soldier, statesman and co-Emperor, a native of the province of Moesia (in modern Serbia). He briefly co-ruled with Constantius II after the murder of Constans in 350.</skos:definition>
